### 1/12 `parser_grammar_io`

> "Implement the grammar-reporting helpers `check_rules` and `check_set` so extracted rules and symbol sets are printed **in the expected order and format**."

Already present; the robustness improvement is the empty-input guard in both (a blank line after `提取文法规则：` is unreadable and happens for real whenever `load_file` fails, since `main` ignores the empty return).

```cpp
void check_rules(const vector<rule> rules) {
	//按提取顺序逐条输出文法规则
	cout << "提取文法规则：" << endl;
	if (rules.empty()) {
		//文法文件为空或者书写格式有误时给出提示，避免只打印一个空行
		cout << "    （未提取到任何文法规则，请检查文法文件的书写格式）" << endl << endl;
		return;
	}
	for (unsigned int i = 0; i < rules.size(); i++) {
		cout << "    " << rules[i] << endl;
	}
	cout << endl;
}
template <class T>
void check_set(set<T> set_, string tip) {
	//按集合内部的有序性依次输出各个元素
	cout << tip << "：" << endl;
	cout << "    ";
	if (set_.empty()) {
		//空集合同样给出提示，方便对照检查提取结果
		cout << "（空）" << endl << endl;
		return;
	}
	for (typename set<T>::iterator it = set_.begin(); it != set_.end(); it++) {
		if (it != set_.begin()) {
			cout << "  ";
		}
		cout << *it;
	}
	cout << endl << endl;
}
```

Clause map: *"expected order"* — `check_rules` walks `rules` in extraction order (`for i < rules.size()`), `check_set` walks `set<T>` in its own sorted order (`begin()..end()`), which is what produces `提取非终结符：A  E  H  M`. *"format"* — 4-space indent per rule, two spaces between set members, blank line after each block so the four report blocks separate. Guards satisfy the robustness ask.

