### 5/12 `parser_follow_core`

> "…scan rule bodies for the target non-terminal, use **suffix FIRST sets** when available, **recurse to parent FOLLOW sets at rule ends**, and **always add `#`**."

```cpp
//求非终结符non_terminal的Follow集，visiting记录当前正在求解的非终结符，防止文法中的递归导致死循环
static set<char> followOf(const char non_terminal, const vector<rule>& rules, set<char>& visiting) {
	set<char> result;
	result.insert('#');//约定输入串结束符“#”总是可以出现在非终结符的后面
	visiting.insert(non_terminal);
	for (unsigned int i = 0; i < rules.size(); i++) {
		for (unsigned int j = 0; j < rules[i].right.size(); j++) {
			const string& part = rules[i].right[j];
			for (unsigned int k = 0; k < part.length(); k++) {
				if (part[k] != non_terminal) {
					continue;//该候选式的这个位置上不是要找的非终结符
				}
				//紧跟其后的符号串决定它的Follow集，空后缀的First集约定为“@”
				set<char> visiting_first;
				set<char> first = firstOf(part.substr(k + 1), rules, visiting_first);
				bool has_epsilon = false;
				for (set<char>::iterator it = first.begin(); it != first.end(); it++) {
					if (*it == '@') {
						has_epsilon = true;//后缀能推出空串，还要看规则左部的Follow集
					}
					else {
						result.insert(*it);
					}
				}
				if (!has_epsilon) {
					continue;//后缀推不出空串，该处出现不再有别的贡献
				}
				//位于规则右部末尾（或其后缀能推出空串）时，规则左部的Follow集并入
				if (visiting.count(rules[i].left) > 0) {
					continue;//该非终结符正处在求解过程中，再递归下去就会陷入死循环
				}
				set<char> sub = followOf(rules[i].left, rules, visiting);
				for (set<char>::iterator it = sub.begin(); it != sub.end(); it++) {
					result.insert(*it);
				}
			}
		}
	}
	visiting.erase(non_terminal);
	return result;
}
F_set findFollow(const char non_terminal, vector<rule> rules) {
	F_set f_set;
	f_set.is_first = false;
	f_set.left = non_terminal;
	set<char> visiting;
	f_set.right = followOf(non_terminal, rules, visiting);
	return f_set;
}
```

Clause map, clause by clause:
* *"scan rule bodies for the target non-terminal"* — the triple loop `i`/`j`/`k` with `if (part[k] != non_terminal) continue;`, so **multiple occurrences in one candidate** are all handled (needed for `A::=Ba B::=Ab|@`-shaped grammars).
* *"use suffix FIRST sets when available"* — `firstOf(part.substr(k + 1), …)`, non-`@` members inserted.
* *"recurse to parent FOLLOW sets at rule ends"* — `part.substr(k+1)` of a final occurrence is `""`, whose FIRST is `{@}` by the `all_epsilon` rule, so the end-of-rule case and the nullable-suffix case go down the *same* branch: `followOf(rules[i].left, …)`. No special-casing needed.
* *"always add `#`"* — the very first statement, `result.insert('#')`, before any early return path.
* `f_set.left = non_terminal;` uses `string::operator=(char)`, giving `Follow(M)=…` with a one-character label.

